  "id": "DrugBank_DB01246 - MONDO_grouped_11786_5324_24332",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Alimemazine may be associated with Allergic Rhinitis through indirect pathways involving other conditions. Alimemazine is linked to Hereditary Angioedema, which in turn is associated with Methdilazine, and Methdilazine is linked to Allergic Rhinitis. Similarly, Alimemazine is also associated with Common Cold, which is linked to Potassium Iodide and Chlorcyclizine, both of which are associated with Allergic Rhinitis. These pathways indicate that Alimemazine may influence the development or manifestation of Allergic Rhinitis through intermediate conditions. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of support for this relationship, though the evidence is not strong enough to establish a definitive causal link. The mechanisms underlying these associations are not fully understood, and further research is needed to clarify the role of Alimemazine in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis.",
